## Title: Quartermaster
## Description: Keeps your bags tidy at a merchant: repairs your gear and sells the clutter (marked junk, trash, treasure, looted potions and poisons, monster trophies, green repair kits, Ornate gear of any quality, white gear, companion gear), then tells you in chat what it sold. It quietly opens the loot boxes and money pouches you pick up once you're out of combat, without popping up the loot window, so their contents get sold too; each kind of container is a switch, and writ rewards, curated coffers and Rewards for the Worthy are left for you by default. It also recharges your equipped weapons with soul gems when their charge drops to the percentage you choose (10% by default). Every kind of item is a switch in Settings > Add-Ons > Quartermaster, with traits to keep for armor, weapons, jewelry and companion gear. Never sells locked, stolen or Crown items, anything your characters crafted, gold gear, or gear you'd deconstruct. Items your characters crafted, and set gear with a kept trait, are also hidden from the Sell, deconstruction and Ragpicker lists; click the right stick to show them. Writ items your characters crafted (white gear, glyphs, potions, poisons) are also left out of the bank's Deposit list; press X at the bank to show them. When trading after a dungeon or trial, the item list shows only the drops the other player can take; the left stick shows everything. It also catalogs what you own across characters, the bank, the craft bag and house chests, with a cleanup report in Settings; press X on the bank's Withdraw tab to stack the bank. Formerly Keep My Crafts. Find it useful? Gold donations by in-game mail to @DextrousDigits (Xbox NA or EU) are very welcome.
